sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-quagga-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-quagga-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-equus-quagga-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Equus quagga Holocene Turing wavelength at 1.9 mm (detail s0) — MorphoEval overall 85.6/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the Pass-1 Schnakenberg field (lambda(k_fast) pinned at 1.883 mm, age 0 Ma, Pearson r = 0.997, RMSE = 0.067 mm). The nominal FFT is 2.032 mm, quantization ratio 1.079 against the analytical fastest mode. A rump crop from the same Namutoni photograph has gradient -72.5 deg (stripes nearly horizontal where the pattern wraps the hindquarter) while the simulation stays at +2.5 deg. That mismatch is reported, not fitted away. An anisotropy probe gives k_measured/k_fast of 0.93, 1.00, and 0.73 at aniso 1.5, 3.2, and 8. Seeding the field at k_fast made the wavelength exact and dropped GIF-to-flank CV from 92.1 to 83, so the noise-seeded nominal render is unchanged. Equus scotti remains the equal-diffusion control. Overall 85.6/100 (faithfulness 85.0, reproducibility 87.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 85, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/equus_quagga_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-equus-quagga-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 553458 B, 1512×888 px, artifact_sha256 63bb5de23ed6cd3e54c0be79e5812c07a0a9ce980568ce526d68bb970186e97a (sha256 63bb5de23ed6cd3e54c0be79e5812c07a0a9ce980568ce526d68bb970186e97a), spec_fingerprint c15e608fbebdc00810bdf416a1196b656433143dafaa4373228dabec7a265ec8. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c15e608fbebdc00810bdf416a1196b656433143dafaa4373228dabec7a265ec8; artifact_sha256: 63bb5de23ed6cd3e54c0be79e5812c07a0a9ce980568ce526d68bb970186e97a. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-equus-quagga-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion, Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics, Murray 1981 coat pre-pattern. | Bard 1977: about 0.4 mm spacing, stripes perpendicular to the dorsal line, third week, plains zebra. | Staddon 2024: curvature-dependent diffusion can orient stripes on a 3-D body.; reconstructed_in_script: 1.883 mm is the slot detail length (10^(-2.725) m), pinned to k_fast at gamma 1.15. Growth factor 4.707 from Bard's 0.40 mm is reconstructed. | Pass 2 adds a rump crop and an anisotropy probe. The rump orientation is not reproduced. | Equus scotti is only the equal-diffusion ablation.; transfer_boundary: The photograph is an adult flank and rump. It does not measure the 1.883 mm fetal wavelength. | A straight periodic patch does not transfer to the rump, where stripes turn.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the 1.883 mm length was calipered on a fetus in this loop. | Does not claim the simulation matches rump stripe orientation. | Does not claim a second assessor scored this pass. | Does not claim Equus scotti's coat is known.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Still one assessor. An independent second score was not run.'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R5', 'item': 'Rump stripes are nearly horizontal and the straight-patch model does not follow them. A curvature-dependent diffusivity (Staddon 2024) on a body mesh would be the next mechanism, not a higher anisotropy on this rectangle.'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.856"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, single agent; second assessor not run)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

